course: dictionary
lesson: 8720
title: Guards on watch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sentry is a guard who stands on watch. Their job is to check who comes near a gate, building or camp, and to watch for danger. The word is a noun, so it names a person, or the job itself. «Sentries posted everywhere» tells you that guards were placed at many points, all watching.
explain: Use the clues around the word. In «A meerkat sentry stands guard while the group digs for beetles», the sentry keeps watch while the others feed, so it must be a lookout. The phrase «sentry box» points to a small shelter where a guard stands.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «They've got sentries posted, and they are all armed» still makes sense if you read it as «They've got guards on watch, and they are all armed». Your meaning fits, so you can trust it.
fact: A sentry is a soldier who stands guard at a gate, building or camp.
fact: «Sentry duty» means the job of guarding.
fact: Sentries watch for danger and check who comes and goes.
fact: The guards outside Buckingham Palace stand in sentry boxes.
fact: In stories, sneaking past a sentry is a classic moment of tension.
exercise: «Mole goes out to check on the stoat sentries.» What is a sentry? | A kind of cold chicken | *A guard who stands on watch | A small boat on the river | A song sung at supper
exercise: «A meerkat sentry stands guard while the group digs for beetles.» What is the sentry doing? | Hunting for beetles alone | Sleeping in a burrow | Digging the hardest of all | *Watching for danger while the others dig
exercise: Find the phrase that means the job of guarding. | Dinner party | Stone wall | Garden gate | *Sentry duty
test: «A sentry stood at the gate all night.» Why would a camp post a sentry? | To hold a party for the soldiers | To sell cold chicken and trifle | To make the camp smell nice | *To watch for danger and check who comes near
test: The guards outside Buckingham Palace stand in sentry boxes. Where does a sentry box usually stand? | On the moon | Inside a teacup | Under the sea | *At a gate or building, where a guard can watch
exam: Which word means nearly the same as sentry? | Gardener | *Guard | Singer | Baker
